    "label list of a given quantum circuit", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",
 CellID->993357154,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell["\<\
Basic objects and operations in discrete quantum mechanics naturally lead to \
an application in quantum information and computation. Quantum Information is \
the study of information encoded in quantum systems. Meanwhile, quantum \
computation is the manipulation of quantum information to perform a \
computation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->50259360,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In quantum information, it is often convenient to have a local state \
description of a multiqubit state. For instance, Alice and Bob shared a \
(possibly entangled) quantum state. But, since they are really far away from \
each other, they do not have access to each other state. In such scenario, \
Alice's description of her part of quantum state is described by a \"reduced \
state\" that can be obtained by ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumPartialTrace"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " operation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->680111415,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell["Trace out the second subsystem in a two-qubit state:", "Text",
 CellID->1912025938,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PsiPlus\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->1678275947,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Partial trace can also be applied to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumBasis"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumBasis", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1570109414,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumBasis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->746824257,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Partial transpose is an operation defined for multiple subsystems state in \
which only a specific subsystem is transposed. For instance, if there are two \
subsystems, partial transpose with respect to the first subsystem is defined \
by a map ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], "\[Rule]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1", 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 ". Partial transpose operation is represented by ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumPartialTranspose"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->966663717,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell["Example of partial transpose:", "Text",
 CellID->634665076,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTranspose", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PsiPlus\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->1607396713,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Although partial transpose is not a physical operation (it does not map a \
density matrix to another density matrix), this operation is quite useful for \
detecting entanglement. In particular, it is used to compute logarithmic \
negativity which is commonly used metric to measure entanglement between two \
states. There are several other metrics to measure entanglement such as \
concurrence and entanglement entropy. The calculation of entanglement measure \
is represented by ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEntanglementMonotone"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " function."
}], "Text",
 CellID->171231949,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plotting various entanglement measure for the state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"00"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"]}]], 
    TemplateBox[{"11"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"]
}], "Text",
 CellID->820919957,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumEntanglementMonotone", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<Concurrence\>\""}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  \t", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumEntanglementMonotone", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ",
        "\n", "   ", "\"\<LogNegativity\>\""}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  \t", 
     RowBox[{"QuantityMagnitude", "@", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumEntanglementMonotone", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
        " ", "\n", "    ", "\"\<EntanglementEntropy\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\n", 
    "  ", "\"\<Entaglement monotone of \
\[Alpha]\!\(\*TemplateBox[{\\\"00\\\"},\n\\\"Ket\\\"]\)+ \!\(\*SqrtBox[\(1 - \
\*SuperscriptBox[\(\[Alpha]\), \(2\)]\)]\)\!\(\*TemplateBox[{\\\"11\\\"},\n\\\
\"Ket\\\"]\)\>\""}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Alpha]\>\"", ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Concurrence\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LogNegativity\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\n", "   ", "\"\<Entanglement Entropy\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->1006830744,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To know whether a state is entangled or separable without computing its \
measure, ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEntangledQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " is used."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1175763064,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell["\<\
Checking whether a subsystem 1 and 3 is entangled in \"W\" state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1074416020,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumEntangledQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<W\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "3", "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->2143439988,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In quantum information, there exist notions of distance between quantum \
state such as fidelity, trace distance, Bures angle, et cetera. One may \
compute distance between two quantum state using various metrics by ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumDistance"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1933756212,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["\<\
Measuring trace distance between a pure state and a mixed state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->943735407,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumDistance", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   " ", "\"\<BuresAngle\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->865519937,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell["\<\
Wolfram quantum framework also supports Schmidt decomposition and spectral \
decomposition.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->845186625,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell["Example of Schmidt decomposition:", "Text",
 CellID->14312863,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"state", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PhiPlus\>\"", "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<SchmidtBasis\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"state", "[", "\"\<Basis\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Association\>\"", 
   "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "@", "Normal"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"state", "[", "\"\<Amplitudes\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->315698450,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell["Example of spectral decomposition:", "Text",
 CellID->1751204118,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"diagState", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<SpectralBasis\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"diagState", "[", "\"\<Amplitudes\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->2116603297,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lastly, one may create a list of many quantum operators. A quantum circuit \
is represented by the symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->530919167,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell["\<\
Example for the construction of quantum circuit without measurement:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1242319925,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", ",", " ", "\[Theta]", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<YY\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<SWAP\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<SX\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<P\>\"", "[", "\[Phi]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<T\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<NOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<BitFlip\>\"", "[", "p", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Braid\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]", ",", " ", "p"}], "}"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"qc", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->1600082692,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "When there is no measurement in the circuit, its action on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumState"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumState", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " would return another ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumState"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumState", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1091979148,ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "3"}], ",", " ", "\[Pi]", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "5"}]}], "]"}], "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->1239660989,ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell["Add measurement into the circuit:", "Text",
 CellID->234435634,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"qc", "/*", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"qc2", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->417968184,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "When there is measurement in the circuit, its action on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumState"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumState", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " would return ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1274591649,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"N", "[", 
   RowBox[{"qc2", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "3"}], ",", " ", "\[Pi]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "5"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->1243964799,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell["Decomposition of CNOT:", "Text",
 CellID->1828403510,ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]"}], "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",",
       " ", "\"\<CZ\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}]}], "}"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"qc", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->623026911,ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "qc", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<CNOT\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->308489360,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", 
      " ", "\"\<RootSWAP\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<RZ\>\"", "[", "\[Pi]", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<RootSWAP\>\"",
       ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<RZ\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       "2"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"qc", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->387004599,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "qc", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<CNOT\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->1976158344,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell["\<\
A quantum gate for the magic basis transformation (transforming 2 qubit \
computational basis to the Bell basis):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1232186413,ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", "\"\<Magic\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"qc", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:= ",
 CellID->655687319,ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<00\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PhiPlus\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:= ",
 CellID->1589358908,ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<10\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"I", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PsiPlus\>\"", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:= ",
 CellID->1191517648,ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<01\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"I", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PhiMinus\>\"", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:= ",
 CellID->960670710,ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qc", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<11\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PsiMinus\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:= ",
 CellID->1307080411,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

